@startuml
title Schatten - Same-Origin OIDC Login And Application Session

actor Browser
participant "Frontend / Caddy\n(one public origin)" as Caddy
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "Configured OIDC provider\nAuthentik: local\nEntra: production direct" as Provider
database PostgreSQL as DB

note over Provider
  TASK-040 may federate local Authentik to Entra
  through a separate local app registration.
  That upstream hop is not the production direct client.
end note

Browser -> Caddy : GET /api/v1/auth/login?return_to=/workspace
Caddy -> API : Fixed Host/proto and trusted client IP
API -> DB : Store hashed state + browser binding, nonce, PKCE
API --> Browser : 302 provider authorization URL\nHttpOnly pre-auth cookie
Browser -> Provider : Authorization Code + PKCE login
Provider --> Browser : Redirect with code + state
Browser -> Caddy : GET /api/v1/auth/callback?code=...&state=...
note right of Caddy
  Access log replaces code, state,
  error and error_description values
  with REDACTED.
end note
Caddy -> API : Callback with fixed proxy headers
API -> DB : Atomically consume browser-bound transaction
API -> Provider : Redeem code with confidential client + verifier
Provider --> API : Validated identity claims
API -> DB : Resolve permanent (issuer, subject)\nCreate hashed opaque application session
API --> Browser : 303 clean local path\nSecure HttpOnly SameSite=Strict cookie
Browser -> Caddy : GET SPA and /api with session cookie
Caddy -> API : Same-origin /api request
API -> DB : Reload active User and session
API --> Browser : Application data only; no provider token

@enduml
